{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-93685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}+{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=1,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+(-1)=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8f9125232d13328071e8a103a05791336757a26518988be86e537aaccad4264"} {"question" "q-93685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8f9125232d13328071e8a103a05791336757a26518988be86e537aaccad4264"} {"question" "q-93982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-93982" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(3){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ -3{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(3{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-3{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8f9125232d13328071e8a103a05791336757a26518988be86e537aaccad4264"} {"question" "q-94004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =0{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-3){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=3,$ and $c=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+3+2=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8f9125232d13328071e8a103a05791336757a26518988be86e537aaccad4264"} {"question" "q-94057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-94057" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-140853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-140853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 5+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =30+6-15+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-140853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e8f9125232d13328071e8a103a05791336757a26518988be86e537aaccad4264"} {"question" "q-140853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-140853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "42"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"} {"question" "q-140853" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "21"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069962/state.json" "file_sha256" "cda76b04c0a313435261e67f3c746a0dca068667bf3bb372d4b032c96cd59146"}] "usage" {"q-93685" [] "q-94004" []} "basis" 2469 "retractions" [[17592186162517 :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatri